        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "C. 0.86 ACRE SITE SUBJECT TO PLANNING PERMISSION \r\n\r\nBrilliantly located site, being sold subject to Planning Permission, just a few minutes drive from the villages of Ballinamuck, Cloone and Drumlish. Situated in the heart of the fishing district at Gortletteragh, this site is just a ten-minute drive from Lough Rynn Castle & Hotel, as well as Mohill Town, while the Keeldra Lake Trail and swimming amenity is also close by. The historic village of Ballinamuck is just 5 minutes away.\r\n\r\nThe property is situated on the county border of Leitrim and Longford, 6km north of Drumlish Village and about 10 mins drive from Mohill Town.\r\nCattan is a peaceful countryside setting, a short drive to Longford, Carrick-on-Shannon and the N4/M4 for easy commuting access to the Capital. \r\n\r\nThe property is just a few miles off the N4 national route, as well as being within one hour of Sligo and less than 100 minutes to Dublin City. A daily commute to the Capital is quite common with some locals.\r\n\r\n(Planning permission previously granted- lapsed in 2010)\r\n\r\nFolio Number: LM18816F\r\n\r\nGPS Coordinates: 53.88194267081337, -7.753079009435077"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious site SPP– c. 0.86 acres\r\n\r\nWithin 30 mins drive to Carrick on Shannon, Cavan & Longford\r\n\r\nDromod Train Station 15 minutes\r\n\r\n20 Minute drive to Longford Train Station\r\n\r\n7 Trains per day on the Dublin-Sligo Line\r\n\r\nCommute to Dublin- 1 hour & 30 mins\r\n\r\nJust a 5-minute drive to Drumlish village\r\n\r\nNote:\r\nThese contents do not constitute an offer or form the basis of any contract. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition etc, are given in good faith and are believed to be correct. Any intending purchasers should not rely on them and are strongly advised to view the property for themselves. All measurements are approximate, photographs and boundary lines provided are for guidance purposes only. These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer; they do not form any part of a resulting contract."
      }
    ],
